          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1.3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Estimate how many litres of air you breathe in one day. Start by estimating how many breaths you take per minute, and the volume of one breath. Your aim is not to find an exact answer, but a reasonable estimate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.16,
            0.89,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " At rest, we take about 12 – 15 breaths a minute, and there are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "60 \\times 24 = 1440"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " minutes in a day, so we take roughly 18 – 22 thousand breaths, about 20 thousand breaths a day. We also need to find the volume of air in one breath. One way to estimate this is to think that it takes about 4 – 5 breaths to fill a typical rubber party balloon, which when inflated has a volume of about 2 litres. So, one breath is perhaps about 0.5 litre. Hence, we breathe in about 10,000 litres of air a day!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.281,
            0.891,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, it is hard to see if this estimate is reasonable or not. But if we go back to our balloon example, one could blow up a balloon in about 20 s, so maybe we could fill 3 balloons a minute. Multiplying"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.229,
            0.337,
            0.889,
            0.376
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3 balloon2 litres1440 minutes minute balloon day will give about 8640 litres, which"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.376,
            0.89,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "for estimation purposes is reasonably close to our earlier estimate of 10,000 litres. Naturally, we would get extremely tired very quickly after blowing balloons nonstop, unlike normal restful breathing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
